The number of good arrangements is $\binom{p^2 - 1}{p - 1}$, which represents the number of ways to partition the set $\{1, 2, \ldots, p^2\}$ into $p$ non-empty subsets. Each such partition corresponds to a unique matrix where the positions form a partition, ensuring that the operations can transform the matrix into a zero matrix.
