All positive integers $ n \geq 3 $ satisfy the condition that for every permutation $ \sigma $, there exists $ 1 \leq i, j, k \leq n $ such that the triangles $ A_iA_jA_k $ and $ A_{\sigma(i)}A_{\sigma(j)}A_{\sigma(k)} $ are both acute, both right, or both obtuse.
