All positive even integers $ n $ satisfy the condition. For each permutation $ \sigma $, there exists a triangle that is either acute, right, or obtuse. For $ n = 2 $, a square, all triangles formed by vertices are right-angled. For $ n = 4 $, a regular quadrilateral, all triangles are right-angled. For $ n = 6 $, a regular hexagon, there are right-angled triangles, and for all even $ n $, the regular polygon ensures that every triangle formed by vertices has at least one right angle. Thus, all even positive integers $ n $ satisfy the condition.
