The minimal real number $ t $ is $ 120\sqrt{2} $. This is derived from analyzing the maximum possible sum of distances from any point $ Q $ on the boundary of a unit square to a set of 120 points. By considering optimal configurations (e.g., placing all points at the vertices), the maximum sum occurs when $ Q $ is at a vertex, leading to the result $ t = 120\sqrt{2} $. 

