For any function $ f $ satisfying the given conditions, the claim $ \alpha(C) \geq \beta(C) - 1 $ holds for each connected component $ C $ of the graph. By analyzing the worst-case scenario where each element is part of a cycle of size 2 (since $ f(x) \neq x $), we find that $ \alpha(C) = 2 $ and $ \beta(C) = 1 $. Thus, $ \alpha(C) - \beta(C) = 1 $, satisfying the inequality. Since $ X $ has 100 elements, the subset $ B $ that covers all elements must include at least one element from each cycle. Therefore, the minimum $ k $ is $ 99 $.
