Assume that for some $ n $, the LCM of the first $ n $ numbers exceeds $ n^{4040} $. Since all numbers are distinct, the next number $ a_{n+1} $ must be the smallest number not dividing the previous 2020 numbers. If this smallest number is larger than $ n $, then all numbers larger than $ n $ can be added to the sequence.  
This is because the LCM of the first $ n+1 $ numbers will be greater than $ n^{4040} $, ensuring that no number larger than $ n $ can be excluded. Hence, every number large enough appears in the sequence.
