All functions $ W : \{1, \dots, n\}^2 \to \mathbb{R} $ satisfying the given condition must have the form $ f(a,b) = 1 $ or $ f(a,b) = -1 $ for all $ a, b \in \{1, \dots, n\} $. This is derived from the symmetry of the equation $ f(a,b)f(b,c) + f(a,c)f(c,b) = 2 $, which holds for all $ a, b, c $, and the requirement that this equation holds for all possible partitions. The function must be symmetric and satisfy $ f(a,b)^2 = 1 $ for all $ a, b $, ensuring consistency across all partitions.
