All functions $ W : \{1, \dots, n\}^2 \to \mathbb{R} $ satisfying the given condition must be constant functions. Specifically, for any $ a, b, c \in \{1, \dots, n\} $, the equation $ f(a,b)f(b,c) + f(a,c)f(c,b) = 2 $ must hold. This equation is satisfied for all distinct $ a, b, c $, and it implies that $ f(a,b) = f(b,c) = f(a,c) = 1 $ for all $ a, b, c $. Therefore, the only function $ W $ that satisfies the condition is the constant function $ W(a,b) = 1 $ for all $ a, b \in \{1, \dots, n\} $.
