All functions $ W : \{1, \dots, n\}^2 \to \mathbb{R} $ satisfying the given condition must be constant functions. Specifically, for any $ a, b, c \in \{1, \dots, n\} $, we have $ f(a,b)f(b,c) + f(a,c)f(c,b) = 2 $, which implies that $ f(a,c) = 0 $ or $ f(c,b) = f(b,a) $. If $ f(a,c) = 0 $ for all $ a \neq c $, this leads to a contradiction unless $ n = 2 $, which contradicts $ n \geq 4 $. Therefore, the only possible function is the constant function $ f(a,b) = 1 $ for all $ a, b $. 

The condition $ \sum_{a \in A} \sum_{b \in B} \sum_{c \in C} W(a,b) W(b,c) = |A| |B| |C| $ holds for all partitions $ A, B, C $, as $ |A| |B| |C| = 1 $ when all sets are size 1, and $ 1^3 = 1 $ in general. Thus, the only valid function is the constant function $ W(a,b) = 1 $.
