The maximum possible value of the sum $\sum_{1 \le i < j \le 12} |P_iP_j|^2$ under the constraint that all pairwise distances are at most 1 is achieved when all points are arranged in a regular 12-gon. In this configuration, each adjacent pair of points has a distance of 1, and the total number of such pairs is $\binom{12}{2} = 66$. Therefore, the smallest positive number $\lambda$ satisfying the condition is $\boxed{66}$.
