All functions $ f: \mathbb{Z}^+ \rightarrow \mathbb{Z}^+ $ satisfying the condition $ f(m \varphi(n^3)) = f(m) \cdot \varphi(n^3) $ for all positive integers $ m, n $ are linear functions of the form $ f(m) = k \cdot m $ for some constant $ k \in \mathbb{Z}^+ $. This follows from the functional equation and the recursive relationships derived from specific cases, such as $ f(4m) = 4f(m) $ and $ f(32m) = 32f(m) $, which confirm that $ f $ is linear.
