The problem reduces to analyzing the game on $ F(8, 1) $, where $ B $ can only empty one of the 8 larger buckets at a time. The key lemma shows that the sum of the largest $ k $ buckets is bounded by $ k \left(1 + \sum_{i=k}^{7} \frac{1}{i} \right) $. By induction, this bound is tight, meaning A can always ensure that at least one bucket is $ \geq k $ at some finite point. Since there are 8 buckets, the maximum $ k $ for which A can always ensure victory is $ \frac{1}{8} $. Thus, all $ k \leq \frac{1}{8} $ satisfy the condition that A can always win the game.
