The problem reduces to analyzing the maximum possible sum of the largest $ k $ buckets after each move. Using induction, we show that for any $ k $, the sum of the largest $ k $ buckets is always less than $ k \cdot \left(1 + \sum_{i=k}^{7} \frac{1}{i} \right) $. Since this bound is strictly decreasing in $ k $, A can always ensure that at least one bucket remains ≥ $ k $, allowing A to win. Thus, A can always win for all positive real numbers $ k $.
